menu "ModESP CAN"

    config MODESP_CAN_ENABLE
        bool "Enable CAN (TWAI) transport"
        default n
        help
            Master switch for the modesp_can component (single TWAI node owner).
            ModESP-CAN v1 (docs/can/ADR-004): SharedState export + event bridge
            between ModESP nodes over classic CAN 2.0B.

            Needs a board.json can_buses entry (tx/rx pins + bitrate) and an
            external CAN transceiver (SN65HVD230, TJA1051T/3 ...) on every node.
            The node's own address: NVS key can/node_id, MAC-derived by default.

            CAN bridge drivers (hardware_type "can", e.g. can_remote) depend on
            this option — their toggles auto-disable when it is off.

    config MODESP_CAN_SELF_TEST
        bool "CAN self-test mode (no-ACK loopback, single-node bench)"
        depends on MODESP_CAN_ENABLE
        default n
        help
            Enables the TWAI self-test + loopback flags: the node receives its
            own frames back without ACK, so the full TX->RX path is verifiable
            on ONE bench device without a transceiver or a second node.
            can.loopback_ok goes true after the first own frame round-trips.

            Never enable on a production bus (no-ACK violates CAN semantics).

endmenu
